+# L08 app-container Foundation discriminator — draft01
+
+Author: `/root/native_fix_review`. **NOT EXECUTED, NOT ADOPTED.** This is a small
+additive adapter for a separately reviewed future composition over functional
+companion02. Existing strict L08 and companion01/02 remain unchanged. No production
+source, storage option, entitlement, receipt, test count or release gate is edited.
+
+## Question
+
+Compare direct Objective-C Foundation calls in the actual owned Debug app sandbox
+with the earlier standalone native CLI control03. Both use the same eight native
+operations and eight ordered metadata checkpoints. A new synthetic Application
+Support sibling is the only fixture authority; no snapshot, rejoin, Documents,
+Keychain, preference, or player-state path is read or modified.
+
+The Foundation image UUID is an installed-runtime observation, not a binding to
+public Foundation source or proof of lock-state enforcement. Missing/non-Complete
+metadata remains visible. No result from this adapter can satisfy or waive strict
+L08, physical-device Data Protection, functional recovery, or Store requirements.
+
+## Integration hooks (root review/adoption still required)
+
+Exact caller contracts and finalization requirements: `ROOT_INTEGRATION.md`.
+
+1. Retain the existing companion02 source copy and all assertions. After its
+   original `inspect_copied_manifest`, apply the additive adapter to that exact
+   owned copy. Revalidate every inherited file hash and the complete input list.
+2. The adapter adds one Objective-C source and bridge header to the app target,
+   with the bridge enabled only for Debug. It appends a Swift button/result and
+   XCTest helper, and adds one call on **existing readiness boot1**, after native
+   geometry/context observation but before its original health button. The
+   actual environment key is `PARLOR_READINESS_BOOT`, verified in both producer
+   and XCTest. Existing eight health, thirteen storage, three host boots and the
+   same five XCTest methods remain required and independently classified.
+3. Fixture execution is explicit and one-shot; remount/rapid-tap/repeated calls
+   cannot rerun it. Native work uses a utility queue, not the UI thread. Original
+   process/token/UDID/scenario guards and root-owned build/finalization lane remain.
+4. Preserve the new bounded `parlor-l08-app-foundation.json` (or closed diagnostic
+   failure receipt) before later verification can throw. This must happen even
+   after an unsuccessful XCTest, alongside—not instead of—existing receipts.
+5. Bind native main/code UUIDs to the exact built/installed image inventories,
+   and compiled context/control/template hashes to the copied-source manifest.
+   Where available, independently cross-check the first health process/boot/token.
+   Keep collection, image provenance, executed XCTest, and cleanup statuses distinct.
+6. Preserve only compact evidence. Existing outer owned-device cleanup remains
+   mandatory even if the fixture hangs or inner cleanup fails. The adapter never
+   signals processes, selects a device, launches a tool, or cleans a host directory.
+
+## Native fixture and finalization
+
+The native observer checks Debug/arm64/iOS Simulator at compile time, exact app
+identity and runtime, actual-vs-expected UDID, readiness boot1, token/boot UUIDs,
+and canonical container under the compiled approved device-set root. It uses the
+same `NSApplicationSupportDirectory` API as production to find the parent, but an
+exclusive token/boot-named private sibling for all mutations. It never changes
+process umask or protection policy for the real store.
+
+Observed operation order is unchanged from control03: create Complete directory;
+read metadata; exclude directory; read; Atomic|Complete write; read; exclude file;
+read; explicit directory Complete setter; read; direct Complete write; read;
+default Atomic write; read; explicit file Complete setter; read. Directory NSURL
+protection queries are intentionally absent; that URL key is regular-file only.
+
+Cleanup is attempted in native `@finally`, confined to exact inode/UID/device-
+attested synthetic parent/root/child and the three fixed file names. No recursive
+or prefix-based removal, symlink following, foreign-root adoption, or fallback.
+Unknown/replaced entries are retained and reported for outer owned-device cleanup.
+An interrupted/hung process cannot emit collection success; root's existing exact
+app/device lifetime finalizer remains the cancellation boundary.
+
